      "id": "bvmid2-003",
      "description": "Safety code half for fingerprint 00 01 .. 1f: 6 groups of 5 digits (SHA-512 iterated 5200 times)",
      "provenance": {
        "file": "app/src/test/java/com/example/bluetoothtest/IdentityVerificationTest.kt",
        "class": "IdentityVerificationTest",
        "line": 570,
        "method": "safetyCodeIsSymmetricStableAndPairSpecific"
      },
      "inputs": {
        "fingerprint": "000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f101112131415161718191a1b1c1d1e1f"
      },
      "expected": {
        "half": "91662 04557 05960 21671 25144 22586"
      },
      "expected_literal": true,
      "kind": "derive",
      "notes": "h1 = SHA-512('BluetoothVideoMesh/IdentityVerification/SafetyCode/2' || fp); h(i+1) = SHA-512(h(i) || fp) up to h5200; group g (0..5) = big-endian 40-bit integer of bytes 5g..5g+4 modulo 100000, zero-padded to 5 digits. The test comment says the values were computed independently with Python hashlib; tools/discovery_crypto.py safety_half() reproduces both."
    },
